I've done some thinking, already, on random level generation.  I think
it would be a simple job to come up with new types of random Nethack
levels -- the problem, for me at least, is deciphering the Nethack
sources to the point where I, who has some experience with C but not a
great deal, could get them implemented without breaking half the game.

A few months (years?) ago I posted here about the possibility of doing
this within the confines of the already-existing special level code,
by scrambling the locations of doors on a pre-drawn level.  I think
from a gameplay standpoint that could be made to work almost as well
as a "traditional" level, but from the player's perspective it'd look
a bit kludgy so I abandoned that line of thinking.  I'm considering
picking it up again, however.

On a recent google search for Nethack patches I found the Nethack
"scripting language" for the level builder from 3.4.2.  I'm rather
excited about the possibility there for if/then structures in level
files, but it doesn't seem to have been updated for 3.4.3.  I'm hoping
this is because the Dev Team has tapped it for 3.5/4.0.

Dammit, now I'm all hyped up about the possibility of making new kinds
of Nethack levels.  Does anyone out there have any special insight
into the way Nethack stores levels & the various rooms, etc. that go
into it?  Maybe the author of that patch, isn't his e-mail address
included....?

- John H.

